---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { appConfig } from '../../../app.config'

const description = 'What this site stores about an account, how long it is kept, and how to delete it.'
const canonical = new URL('/privacy', appConfig.app.url).href
---

<Base title={`Privacy · ${appConfig.app.name}`} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <main id="content" class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      An account stores the name and email you submit, a password hash, and the sessions you open.
    </p>
    <h2>Account data</h2>
    <p>
      Registration stores your name, email address, and a password hash. The password itself is not
      stored. A session is a random id kept in an HttpOnly cookie. The database stores only a hash
      of that id, plus when the session was created and when it expires. Sessions last seven days.
    </p>
    <p>
      A password reset stores a hash of a one-hour link, not the link itself. Sign-in, sign-out, and
      account deletion write an audit row with the user id and the action. The audit row does not
      include the email address or the password.
    </p>
    <h2>How long it is kept</h2>
    <p>
      The account, password hash, and sessions stay until you delete the account from
      <a href="/app/settings">settings</a>. Deletion removes the user and every session. The audit
      row for that deletion remains, with the user id only. Public pages still do not read the
      database.
    </p>
    <h2>Export</h2>
    <p>
      Settings can download the name, email, account id, and session times. The download does not
      include the password hash or session secrets. The <a href="/terms">terms</a> describe the
      site as published.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
